in the left graph indicates that a longer prediction interval forces the model to prioritize
     信




effects with potentially longer durations, such as "score advantage". On the contrary,
short-term events like "net point won", "ace" gain less weight. In the right graph, the
model trained on 50% appears notable changes, likely due to the altered distribution of
    微




matches. On the other hand, the model trained with 70% of the data remained stable,
indicating a threshold of data sufficiency.




