7.3   Conclusion
                                ：

                                                            els
    In this paper, we establish our momentum predictor through a two-step process.
                               号
Initially, we develop a naive binomial model aimed at recovering the "ideal" state of



                                                          od
the game. Subsequently, the residual of its prediction is utilized as the label for our
momentum predictor, the dual-temporal Bayesian network. This model framework,
                           众


demonstrated to be highly generalizable and robust, allows us to uncover the latent
                                                         m
systems underlying observable sports games.
